# Runtime state and host-managed worktrees
.pi/orchestrator/
.pi/worktree/
.pi/worktree-state/
# GC-2026-044: sub-agent-owned runtime state. These sit OUTSIDE
# `.pi/orchestrator/` on purpose (memory rule #23 keeps that namespace
# L3-only), so they need their own entries here — a diagnostic is a
# post-mortem about one machine's run and must never reach a commit.
# `**/` matters: a sub-agent's cwd is often a package dir, not the repo
# root, and the root-anchored form above would miss `pi-subagents/.pi/`.
**/.pi/diagnostics/
**/.pi/worktree-leases/
# Project-local failure-mode catalog override (design §2.1). The SHIPPED
# default at `pi-subagents/src/data/failure-modes.v1.yaml` IS committed.
**/.pi/failure-modes.yaml
# `.sages/` is kept gitignored as a working area for in-flight design
# work (e.g. `pi/.sages/designs/<date>-<topic>.md` brainstorming
# drafts, `pi/.sages/workspace/execution.yaml` legacy qiaochui
# decomposition output, `.sages/snapshots/<id>.bak` from the planned
# AFT migration's `aft/safety.ts` T7 task). The active 4-tool
# orchestrator writes ONLY to `.pi/orchestrator/` — see
# `pi/src/tools/orchestrator/types.ts:198` for `ORCHESTRATOR_DIR`.
.sages/

# Plan files (generated)
.plan/

# Worktrees (isolated development)
.worktrees/
tool/

